  "title": "Upgrade Prompt Editor with Embedded Code Regions",
  "branch": "feature/prompt-editor-embedded-regions",
  "summary": "Convert the prompt box from a plain TextBox to a RichTextBox so it can host collapsible embedded code regions, add triple-backtick fence creation/collapse, and add Up/Down boundary navigation across those regions \u2014 all without regressing ordinary plain-text typing, voice dictation, or existing transcript code-block styling.",
  "tasks": [
    {
      "taskId": "PROMPTEDITOR-20261012-001",
      "title": "Convert PromptTextBox to RichTextBox foundation",
      "description": "Replace the existing TextBox-based prompt editor control with a RichTextBox-based implementation that preserves the current plain-text typing experience and voice dictation integration.\n\n## Observable outcome\n\nThe prompt editor renders and behaves as a RichTextBox internally while ordinary plain-text usage (typing, placeholder/watermark display, auto-grow/resize, scrollbar behavior, selection highlight, caret and line rendering) is intended to remain visually and behaviorally equivalent to the prior TextBox. Because a TextBox\u2192RichTextBox control-type migration can introduce subtle rendering differences that automated tests cannot truthfully rule out, final confirmation of plain-text appearance/interaction parity is a human observation recorded at the plan\u0027s approval gate rather than a claim made by this task alone.\n\n## Consumers\n\nTasks 002 and 003 build embedded-region creation, collapse, and boundary navigation on top of this RichTextBox foundation; the existing voice dictation pipeline continues to target this control.\n\n## Constraints\n\nDo not change the public surface voice dictation uses to insert text. Preserve existing data-binding and focus behavior used elsewhere in the prompt workflow.",
      "dependsOn": [],
      "priority": "high",
      "status": "complete",
